        "fr": "Floette",
        "it": "Floette",
        "ja": "フラエッテ",
        "ko": "플라엣테",
        "ja-Hrkt": "フラエッテ",
        "zh-Hans": "花叶蒂",
        "zh-Hant": "花葉蒂"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Floette floats along holding its flower like a parasol, tending wilting flowerbeds and celebrating new blooms, and it never forgives anyone who tramples one. It can't use moves alone: it first syncs with its flower through wavelengths of light to share their power. One Floette carrying a black-and-red Eternal Flower is at the heart of the story in Pokémon X and Y and Legends: Z-A.",
        "guide": "Floette is a Fairy-type Pokémon, the middle stage of Flabébé's line, found in five flower colours. It looks after flowerbeds and draws its power from the flower it holds. A unique Eternal Flower Floette belonging to AZ appears in X and Y and Legends: Z-A, and only it can Mega Evolve.",
        "tagline": "A fairy gardener with a flower for a parasol",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Floette (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Floette_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
