        "ja-Hrkt": "フラージェス",
        "zh-Hans": "花洁夫人",
        "zh-Hant": "花潔夫人"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Florges claims its territory by growing gorgeous flower gardens, said to heal body and spirit, and it ruthlessly punishes anyone who vandalises them, even if they beg. Castle lords once kept Florges to tend their gardens, and one is recorded as living over 300 years. Its flowery collar recalls the towering, decorated pouf hairstyles of the 18th century.",
        "guide": "Florges is a Fairy-type Pokémon, the final form of Flabébé, found in five flower colours. It creates beautiful flower gardens, draws power from flowers, and has the highest Special Defense of any Fairy type. It is long-lived, and all Florges are female.",
        "tagline": "A fairy who guards its garden for three hundred years",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Florges (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Florges_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
